<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title>Opensource on metafunctor</title><link>https://metafunctor.com/tags/opensource/</link><description>Research Engineer &amp; Computer Scientist - Machine Learning, Statistical Computing, Open Source Development</description><language>en-us</language><managingEditor>lex@metafunctor.com (Alex Towell)</managingEditor><webMaster>lex@metafunctor.com (Alex Towell)</webMaster><lastBuildDate>Sat, 03 Jan 2026 01:14:42 -0600</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://metafunctor.com/tags/opensource/" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><image><url>https://metafunctor.com/images/og-image.jpg</url><title>metafunctor</title><link>https://metafunctor.com/</link></image><item><title>Crier: Cross-Post Your Content Everywhere</title><link>https://metafunctor.com/post/2025-12-16-crier/</link><pubDate>Tue, 16 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://metafunctor.com/post/2025-12-16-crier/</guid><description>Crier is a CLI tool for cross-posting content to dev.to, Ghost, WordPress, Bluesky, Mastodon, and more. Now available on PyPI.</description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I&rsquo;ve published <strong>crier</strong> to <a href="https://pypi.org/project/crier/">PyPI</a> - a command-line tool for cross-posting content to multiple platforms simultaneously.</p>
<p>Like a town crier announcing news across the land, crier broadcasts your content to dev.to, Ghost, WordPress, Hashnode, Medium, Bluesky, Mastodon, Threads, Telegram, Discord, and more.</p>
<h2 id="installation">Installation</h2>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="line"><span class="cl">pip install crier
</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="the-problem">The Problem</h2>
<p>If you maintain a blog and want to reach audiences on multiple platforms, you face tedious manual work: copy content to dev.to, create a Bluesky post with a link, toot on Mastodon, post to your Discord server, etc. Each platform has its own interface, API, and quirks.</p>
<h2 id="the-solution">The Solution</h2>
<p>Crier lets you publish once and distribute everywhere:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="line"><span class="cl"><span class="c1"># Publish to multiple platforms at once</span>
</span></span><span class="line"><span class="cl">crier publish post.md --to devto --to bluesky --to mastodon --to discord
</span></span></code></pre></div><p>That single command:</p>
<ul>
<li>Publishes the full article to dev.to</li>
<li>Creates a Bluesky post with title, description, and link</li>
<li>Toots on Mastodon with hashtags from your tags</li>
<li>Posts an announcement embed to your Discord server</li>
</ul>
